    "updated_at": "2026-11-25T07:03:48Z",
    "body": "fix on issue/3331-turning-start-exit · PR #3981 · pinned by `the_first_pass_starts_at_the_start_pick`, `the_last_pass_leaves_at_the_exit_pick`, `an_impossible_pick_is_refused_by_name`, `a_pick_whose_move_crosses_the_part_or_the_stock_is_refused_by_name`, `threading_keeps_its_start_law_and_says_so_by_name`, `undo_and_redo_restore_the_path`, `mcp_edit_operation_sets_the_turning_picks_and_undo_clears_them` (app, `start_exit_shared`), `turning::start_exit::tests::*` (motion) · merges when reviewed\n\nThis PR is slice 1: Facing, Profile Rough and Profile Finish. Its commit says `Refs #3331`, so the merge does not close this issue. These kinds are not done: Groove Rough, Groove Finish, Part, Chamfering, Taper Turning, Multi-Pass Turning, Form Turning, Boring Turning. They keep the \"owed\" row. A next slice can use `turning::with_picks` and add its arm in `KindInfo::pick`.\n\n@NeoTech: this is yours to take back at any time - say so here and we stop.\n",
    "author_association": "COLLABORATOR",
    "pin": null,
